# `FLOWCHART-ROLE-KEYWORDS`: `shape=` on a role line overrides the DRAWING and nothing else. The
# role stays the model (core §12.7 — presentation is not meaning on its own),
# so every node below still carries its role while carrying a shape the role
# would not have derived. The reverse also holds: `node … shape=diamond` has
# NO role, which is the whole reason the vocabulary exists.
figdown 0.2 flowchart
decision  wide  "Which case?" shape=ellipse
process   round "Normalize"   shape=rounded
terminator boxy "Halt"        shape=box
node      plain "Look-alike"  shape=diamond
flow down
flowline wide -[a]-> round
flowline wide -[b]-> boxy
flowline round -> plain
